\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God moves in a mysteriuos way
\par His wonders to perform;
\par He points His footsteps in the sea,
\par And rides upon the storm.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Deep in unfathomable mines
\par Of never-falling skill
\par He treasures up His bright designs,
\par And works His sovereign will.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Ye fearful saints, fresh courage take,
\par The clouds ye so much dread
\par Are big with mercy, and shall break 
\par In blessings on your head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Judge not the Lord by feeble sense,
\par But trust Him for His grace;
\par Behind a frowning providence
\par He hides a smiling face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. His purposes will ripen fast,
\par Unfolding every hour;
\par The bud may have a bitter taste,
\par But sweet will be the flower.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Behind unbelief is sure to err,
\par And scan His work in vain;
\par God is His own interpreter,
\par And He will make it plain.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

